WEBVTT

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.870
VOICE BOX:
There's a snake in my boot.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:19.230
I'd like to join your posse, boys,
but first I'm gonna sing a little song.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.390
A sheriff!

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.870
Move over, Mr. Pricklepants.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.630
We have a guest.
You want some coffee?

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:32.630
It's good for you. But don't drink
too much, or you'll have to... Have to...

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:34.830
Be right back!

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.630
Psst! Hey, hello? Hi. Excuse me.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:38.830
(SHUSHING)

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.590
Can you tell me where I am?

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.070
The guy's just asking a question.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.230
Well, excuse me.
I'm trying to stay in character.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:46.670
(SNIFFS DRAMATICALLY)

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:49.750
My name's Buttercup.
You've met Baron von Shush.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.070
Hello, I'm Trixie.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.670
(BOTH SHUSHING)

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:54.670
Guys, hey. Guys, look,
I don't know where I am.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:58.070
We're either in a café in Paris
or a coffee shop in New Jersey.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.110
I'm pretty sure
I just came back from the doctor

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:02.110
with life-changing news.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:04.590
We do a lot of improv here. Just stay
loose, have fun, you'll be fine.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:05.750
(TOILET FLUSHING)

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.750
-No, no, no, no. I...
-Who wants lunch?

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.430
Bee-boop-bee-boop.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:14.310
It has a secret ingredient. Jelly beans.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:17.510
VOICE BOX:
Somebody's poisoned the water hole.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:21.110
(GASPS) Poison?
Who would do such a mean thing?

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.270
(CACKLES)

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:30.190
(EXCLAIMS) The scary witch! Look out!
She's using her witch-y powers!

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.190
"I know where to hide."

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:38.310
She'll never find us in here.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.630
What's wrong?

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:41.790
(EXCLAIMS)

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:45.390
She found us! We need a spaceship
to get away from the witch!

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:48.310
-You're doing great!
-Are you classically-trained?

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.990
Look, I just need to know
how to get out of here!

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:51.470
There is no way out.

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:52.630
(GASPS)

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.070
Just kidding. Door's right over there.

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:57.230
Well, cowboy, you just
jumped right in, didn't ya? I'm Dolly.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:58.550
-Uh, Woody.
-Woody?

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.390
Really? You're gonna stick with that?

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.070
'Cause now's your chance to change it,
new room and all.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:04.830
That's coming from a doll named Dolly.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.510
-Who's the new guy?
-Are you a real cowboy?

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.750
-Well, actually...
-'Course he's not, pea brain.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.990
-He don't even have a hat.
-I do too have... (GASPS) My hat!

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.350
-Told ya.
-BONNIE: I found a spaceship!

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:17.750
Showtime.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:20.270
Quick, get in. Fasten your seat belts.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.910
Close your tray tables. Hold on.
It might get a little bumpy.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:27.350
Three, two, one, blastoff!

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:31.750
Yee-haw!

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:35.270
You saved us, cowboy.
You're our hero.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:36.670
(LAUGHING)

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.910
(TOYS GROANING)

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.590
Oh, I got a kink in my slink.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.190
(GROANING IN DISGUST)

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.590
(EXCLAIMS) My tail! Where's my tail?

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:54.550
(GROANS)

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:55.870
(GRUNTING)

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.310
Someone need a hand?

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:01.790
-Where's my nose?
-Here it is.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.150
-Here's your arm.
-Give me that. That's mine.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.390
Honey, the mustache?

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:07.230
I don't recall playtime being
quite that strenuous.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:10.630
Andy never played with us like that.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.630
We're just gonna have to
make the best of it.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.470
But these toddlers,
they don't know how to play with us.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:16.910
-They're too young!
-Yeah, they're sticky.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:18.230
Well, we should be
in the Butterfly Room.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.310
MRS. POTATO HEAD:
With the big kids!

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:20.470
MR. POTATO HEAD: That's right.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.230
-Yeah, you said it.
-We'll get this straightened out.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.990
I'll go talk to Lotso
about moving us to the other room.

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.430
Blast. Try that one.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.670
It's locked!

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.790
-Same here.
-Try the windows.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.750
Negatory.
It's a Fenster-Schneckler 380.

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.590
Finest childproof lock in the world.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:41.750
-We're trapped!
-Wait.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:43.110
Did anyone notice the transom?

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.750
Oh, great. How do we get up there?

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:52.270
All right, everyone. On three!
One, two...

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.110
-Three!
-Whoa!

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.350
Let go!

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.310
Go!

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:15.110
(TOYS LAUGHING)

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.990
REX: He did it!
HAMM: Yes, sir!

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:19.550
(LAUGHS) Way to go, Buzz!

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.630
CHUNK: (CHUCKLING) Yeah,
you think they had a fun playtime?

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:25.990
TWITCH: (SHUSHES)
They might hear you.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:27.950
(BARBIE GIGGLING)

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:30.710
-Okay, now you start.
-I...

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:31.950
-Love...
-You.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:34.390
See? That time, I said "love."
Okay, now me first.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:35.550
-Okay, okay, okay.
-KEN: I...

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:36.790
BARBIE: Love...
KEN: You.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:38.910
You see what I mean?
It changes every time.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:40.630
You are so smart.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.350
Come on, Romeo. We're late.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:44.750
BARBIE: I'll wait up for you.
KEN: Kisses!

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:18.030
(TOYS CHATTERING)

